# Ball603 Redirects

# ===== FARMINGTON TIGERS DOMAIN =====
# farmingtontigersnh.com is a pointer, not a second copy of the site. Everything
# on that host is sent to the one canonical home under ball603.com, and these
# sit at the very top because Netlify uses the FIRST rule that matches.
#
# The ! is what makes them win over the static files and the host rewrites
# further down; without it a real file at the requested path would be served
# instead of the redirect.
#
# One consequence worth knowing: a 301 is a PERMANENT redirect and browsers
# cache it hard, for months. If the Tigers site is ever meant to be served from
# its own domain again, anyone who has hit these will keep being bounced long
# after the rules come out. Change them to 302 first if that is on the cards.
# Old service workers. Browsers that visited farmingtontigersnh.com when it
# served pages itself (SportsEngine, or the Tigers site before it moved) still
# have a worker on that origin that answers every visit before the network is
# asked, and sends people to SportsEngine's "page not found". A browser
# re-fetches its worker script on each visit to check for updates; a 301 there
# counts as a failed update and keeps the old worker forever. So these script
# paths get a real file instead: tigers-sw-reset.js, which replaces the old
# worker, clears its caches, unregisters, and sends the tab to ball603.com.
# They must stay ABOVE the 301s below (Netlify uses the first match).
https://farmingtontigersnh.com/sw.js  /tigers-sw-reset.js  200!
https://farmingtontigersnh.com/service-worker.js  /tigers-sw-reset.js  200!
